// policy arm boundary: src/policy/expm1.rs classify routes |x| <= 1 in RAW storage units (raw <= 10^SCALE) to the Series kernel and everything else to ViaExp - an analytic validity wall, not a tuning knob: outside it the series carries no range reduction and either alternates into cancellation (x < 0) or peaks at e^x/sqrt(2*pi*x) (x > 0), and it stops at SERIES_CAP, returning a TRUNCATED value rather than a slow one. These are the last Series-routed and the first ViaExp-routed arguments at each scale - 1 -/+ 10^-S and -1 +/- 10^-S, one ULP either side of the wall on both signs, plus the exact +/-1 that the <= keeps on the Series side. An off-by-one in that raw comparison hands an argument to a kernel that is not valid for it, and only an input adjacent to the wall can see it. These carry no sub-ULP tie structure of their own, but the gen_precision wall still reaches them at the deepest scale, where a value whose two guard digits both happen to be zero reads as exact. A row is graded at EVERY cell whose envelope holds it, not only the one it was derived for, so the binding constraint is that the first deciding digit BELOW the LSB must fall inside the 1233 stored digits at every such cell - at a far deeper scale that is a much later series term. Inputs failing that anywhere were dropped; what remains is decidable at every cell it reaches
