// domain edge - the band where expm1 is defined and exp is NOT: expm1(x) <= MAX needs x <= ln(MAX+1) while exp(x) <= MAX needs x <= ln(MAX), so expm1's domain runs ln(1 + 1/MAX) wider than exp's. Each pair is the smallest and the largest argument representable strictly inside its own cell's band: the first argument at which a composed exp-minus-one overflows the tier, and the last at which expm1 itself does not. ViaExp arm. The band narrows as MAX grows, dropping below one ULP once 10^(2S) < 2^(64N-1), so the LOW-scale cells of every tier cannot host this family at all and are NOT covered by it - only the deepest two or three scales per tier are. Stated as a known gap rather than left silent
