// exact point and sign change: expm1(0) = 0 is the ONLY exact value on the whole domain - e^a is transcendental for every rational a != 0 (Lindemann-Weierstrass), so expm1 is irrational at every other input the golden set can hold, which is why oracle/exactness.py classifies it in the pure-transcendental family. Every rounding mode must return an exact zero here with no directed-mode step. +/-2 are the nearest plain ViaExp anchors either side of the wall - a sign-symmetric pair outside the Series region without being a boundary case itself
