// Trunc non-commutation, power-of-ten argument - negative mirror, completing the block above at m = 250, 290, 306: the three golden scales whose POSITIVE twin +10^-m is carried by the directed-mode guard-step block but whose negative form was absent, leaving D1232<250>, D307<290> and D307<306> with no row at all in the underflow-toward-zero direction. expm1(-10^-m) lands strictly between -10^-m and 0 at S = m, so the truncated coefficient is 0 - which IS the round-05up pivot - and ZeroFiveUp and AwayFromZero both step away from zero to -10^-m while Trunc and Ceiling return exactly 0. Each passes the block's own depth rule: |expm1(-10^-m)| runs a 9-run at digits m+1..2m, a 5 at 2m+1, zeros at 2m+2..3m, and is dense from 3m+1 because 1/6 repeats, so the only blind window is a graded scale S in [2m+1, 3m-1] whose next non-zero digit at 3m+1 falls past the 1233 stored digits; here 3m+1 is 751, 871 and 919, every one of them inside. The remaining uncovered golden scales m = 461, 462, 470, 590, 615 are NOT addable for exactly that reason - each has a graded scale inside its blind window (461, 462, 470 and 590 at S = 1200, 615 at S = 1231) with 3m+1 falling between 1384 and 1846 - so such a row would read as EXACT at that cell and grade every mode alike. They are omitted deliberately, as they already are from the positive block
